From 42f9e3087215d99865f705947d05523b36ebaf42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): review fork counts a replayed, still-current
 skill_view as a read [daveey]

The background-review fork resumes the parent transcript. When the parent
had loaded a skill (e.g. a 90 KB myapp-development SKILL.md) and the
file is unchanged, the fork already holds the exact current content, yet
read-before-write refused its first patch ('content has not been loaded in
this review turn'), forcing a redundant re-view each review.

Before the fork runs, seed the read marks from the history it replays:
a full skill_view result is marked only when it is byte-identical to what
skill_view serves now (same source path). Stale, pruned, stubbed or
non-skill_view copies stay unmarked, so the guard still fires for them.
